 "gates_doc": "W3/W4 — Originate Week 10 NFL lines from the verified official 2026 game log (Weeks 1-9), and refresh the\nskill-vs-luck validation: walk-forward evaluation, proper scoring vs naive baselines, bootstrap CIs, permutation\ntests, multiple-testing control, standings luck decomposition, and the points-only leaderboard (singles, parlays,\nplayer-prop combos) for the extended window W3-W9.\n\nContinuation of session 4bc92a5f's O2/O3/O4 framework (same strategies, same gates), extended to Week 9 data by\nsession e8155046. No sportsbook / market data is used anywhere: every input row comes from an official NFL source\n(nfl.com scores, standings, schedule; Next Gen Stats). Strategies that would need market prices are listed but\ncannot pass gate G8 and are never scored.\n\nPre-registered gates (fixed in code before any result was seen; identical for every strategy):\n  G1 official data   every training/evaluation row is a verified official row (build_gamelog_w10.py fail-closed)\n  G2 no leakage      predictions for week w use only games from weeks < w (asserted at run time)\n  G3 sample size     >= 80 games (singles) | >= 40 independent pairs (parlays) | >= 100 player-games (props)\n  G4 skill           paired bootstrap 95% CI of mean(loss_model - loss_baseline) lies entirely below 0\n  G5 multiplicity    Holm-adjusted one-sided sign-flip permutation p < 0.05 across the whole family\n  G6 stability       mean loss improvement is positive in BOTH halves of the evaluation window\n                     (this refresh: half1 = W3-W6, half2 = W7-W9 — fixed before results were computed)\n  G7 calibration     probability products only: expected calibration error (5 bins) <= 0.10\n  G8 no market data  strategy can be priced and settled without sportsbook odds\nRanking (\"leaderboard\"): strategies passing ALL gates are ranked by the LOWER 95% bound of their skill score\n(% loss reduction vs baseline), so a lucky point estimate cannot buy a medal.\n\nStatus of Week 10 lines: PROSPECTIVE / UNVALIDATED — the W10 slate is played after origination; gates are\nre-evaluated only after W10 finals exist. The already-played W10 Thursday game (WAS 24 NYG 21) is excluded\nfrom line origination and recorded separately.\n",
